        "original_id": "e4056f8b-d637-50d3-9063-81b01a57500d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Jack and Jill, Paper, Children's Digest\n- Places: New York City\n- Topics: children's magazines, fashion, popular culture, nightlife, music, art, film\n\nFacts:\n- Children's Digest was originally titled The Children's Digest and was published from October 1950 to May/June 2009.\n- Jack and Jill is an American bimonthly magazine for children ages 7 to 12, and its title comes from the nursery rhyme Jack and Jill.\n- Paper, stylized as PAPER, is an independent magazine based in New York City that focuses on fashion, popular culture, nightlife, music, art, and film.\n- After Children's Digest ended in May/June 2009, it was merged into Jack and Jill by the same publisher.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "6c864876-d023-575d-8345-f8c289827fb9",
        "text": "Page: Jack and Jill (magazine). Sentence: Jack and Jill is an American bimonthly magazine for children 7 to 12 years old that takes its title from the nursery rhyme of the same name.\nPage: Paper (magazine). Sentence: Paper, stylized as PAPER, is a New York City-based independent magazine focusing on fashion, popular culture, nightlife, music, art and film.\nPage: Children's Digest. Sentence: Children's Digest (originally \"The Children's Digest\") was a children's magazine published from Oct. 1950 to May/June 2009, after which it was merged with \"Jack and Jill\" from the same publisher.",
